3.1.m:
Nandīśvara said:
Countless indeed are the incarnations across the kalpas of the all-pervading Lord of all;
nevertheless, I will speak of them here according to my intellect.

3.6.m:
Śakra said:
"O seeker of a son, I will give you a son born of a womb, subject to death;
otherwise, I will not give one to you, for beings free from death do not exist.

The son said:
Not by austerity, O father, shall I cheat death, nor by knowledge;
by worshipping Mahādeva I shall conquer death, not otherwise.

3.7.m:
Umā said:
You should grant [this] to Nandin, O God of gods, O Parameśvara;
most exceedingly dear to me, O Lord, is this son of Śalāda.
